==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*taglą}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*dek-}}. Cognate with Middle Low German {{m|gml|tagel||twisted whip}}, Old High German {{m|goh|zagal||animal’s tail}} (dialectal German {{m|de|Zagel}}), Old Norse {{m|non|tagl||horse’s or cow’s tail}}, Gothic {{m|got|𐍄𐌰𐌲𐌻||hair of the head}}; and, beyond Germanic, with Old Irish {{m|sga|dūal||lock of hair}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈtæjel/|lang=ang}}

